<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 03-JUN.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 03-JUN.</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Storm Andres, with 40 mph winds, is 270 miles southeast of Acapulco, Mexico, moving north northeast at 7 mph. Top winds are 40 mph and should remain near 40 mph throughout the day Tuesday, as the storm motion becomes more northeast. Pacific coastal areas of Guatemala and eastern Mexico will see gusty winds and heavy rain, with the threat of local flooding.  </p>
<p>There are no further emergency statements at this time.</p>
</text>
